  "scope": "Three public requests at seed 8102. Roof-on exterior, sampled functional room groups and secondary cutaway. This is comparison evidence, not the full house-style acceptance matrix.",
  "findings": [
    "The hipped roof and porch suggest the narrowed fictional timber-house brief, but the repeated Tudor-like wall grid and cottage room layout do not carry that character inside.",
    "Actual rooms use the same high western dining chairs, single bed, rough workbench, metal-band chests and torches as ordinary styles. The target's low furniture, quiet partitions and entry hierarchy are absent.",
    "The default arrival and cooking cameras face large bare wall and floor runs. They are single viewpoints; the cutaway and planned inventory must supplement them.",
    "The large kitchen has generic high tables in open floor, disconnected barrel stand and wall shelving.",
    "Sleeping rooms have a generic bed against plain walls. Storage is isolated crates/chests rather than integrated household storage.",
    "Roof tiers and sheltered thresholds need more purposeful proportions; the large shell remains a broad repeated rectangle."
  ],
